WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.880
A$AP Rocky just posted his latest music video with this scene, which looks like a direct copy of this post that was made on Instagram a few years ago,

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:12.880
except the original person was replaced with A$AP Rocky using AI.

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:20.240
So you could see here that this is the music video, that is the original video, and there is practically no difference.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:27.540
The grass pattern is the same, the shadows are the same, and even if you overlay it, you could see that there's very little to no difference.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:35.580
So the question is, at what point does AI-generated content cross the line into copyright infringement?
